PUBLIC SUPPORT BOUNDARY
=======================

FreeSDN is maintained by its sole owner and developer. Release acceptance gates
and local qualification artifacts are not a third-party audit, a compliance
attestation or a commercial support contract.

Platform: the appliance is qualified only for Linux amd64. ARM64 builds
and ARM64 installation are unsupported by this evidence. Do not publish an ARM64
stable manifest until the runtime, database, media/VPN binaries, restore and
installation gates pass on that architecture. Agent desktop/platform releases
have their own independent qualification and signing requirements.

Deployment: Lite/Pro/Max presets and single-host HA have bounded automated fixture
evidence. The HA Compose overlay offers process/service failover on one host; it
does not provide host-loss protection. Asynchronous replication and every-second
AOF can lose acknowledged writes. No zero-RPO, partition fencing or production
capacity/retention guarantee is made. Sizing figures are planning starting points.

Operations: Proxmox SDN apply remains blocked. Read/stage visibility is not proof
that every write family is supported. Scheduled SLA reports generate PDF/CSV
archives subject to access checks. Opt-in SMTP notices use durable records,
current recipient/actor authorization and bounded safe retries. Existing schedules
remain opted out; uncertain sends are never automatically repeated. Attachments,
external recipients and inbox-delivery confirmation are unsupported. Read
SLA-REPORT-DELIVERY; real-relay/restore/capacity acceptance remains separate.

Existing sites: preserve old images, database/queue volumes and Sentinel state.
Read postgres/UPGRADING, redis/HA-UPGRADING, redis/QUEUE-INVENTORY and
redis/QUEUE-BACKUP-RECOVERY. A passing synthetic restore does not select your
authoritative primary, establish completeness of your backup, reconcile hardware
effects or authorize replay. Coordinated customer migration remains an acceptance
gate. Post-snapshot JWT recovery requires separate signing-key review while vault
keys remain unchanged; see the authentication recovery instructions.

Hardware: prior real Omada, Hikvision, UniFi, TrueNAS and Proxmox use is acknowledged.
Qualify the actual released image digests against each supported firmware/API
version and workflow before making a new-candidate production support claim.
Public VPN NAT/relay/routing/ACL/reconnect acceptance remains separate.

Security: no third-party audit or compliance certification is claimed. Runtime
scans are dated evidence for exact images, not a perpetual absence of vulnerabilities.
The optional UDP collector belongs on a restricted management network with source
firewalling; an IP allowlist is not cryptographic sender authentication. Never
expose its telemetry ports directly to the Internet.

Distribution: a stable release must bind the reviewed source to hosted CI, version,
image digests, SBOMs, signatures/attestations and a clean installation from the
actual published artifacts. Local passing tests do not satisfy publication gates.
